#
# This file is the content STYLE.md §8 has always specified, now on disk. Until
# the ninth round it existed only as a fenced block inside a document, so every
# rule below that claims clang-tidy enforcement (google-explicit-constructor,
# modernize-use-override, the readability-identifier-naming set) was in fact
# enforced by nothing at all -- see the tool-status note at the top of STYLE.md.
#
# Still not wired into CI: there is no check-clang-tidy job, and docs/07 §13
# lists check-cpplint and check-format as release gates that also do not exist.
# Column width in particular has no gate here -- clang-tidy does not check it and
# clang-format is not run in CI -- so tools/check_invariants.py rule C23 covers
# it with a ratchet instead. See that rule's comment.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Checks turned OFF, and why. Each of these is a case where the check is right
# in general and wrong for avbase -- turning it off is a decision, not a
# surrender, so the reason belongs here next to the rule it disables. (Same
# shape as CPPLINT.cfg's -build/c++11.)
#
# -performance-enum-size
#     Wants every enum to spell out a 1-byte underlying type. For the headers
#     under player/public/ -- which the SDK INSTALLS -- that is an ABI change
#     to a published interface, to save three bytes. 48 findings, all of them
#     enums that are passed by value, never arrayed.
#
# -modernize-use-nodiscard
#     Wants [[nodiscard]] on every const member function whose result can be
#     dropped. avbase is full of Chromium-style snake_case() accessors (160
#     findings in one TU), and dropping the result of an accessor is not a
#     failure mode this project has. Satisfying it would put an attribute on
#     every accessor declaration for no read-time benefit.
#
# -google-readability-braces-around-statements
#     Demands braces on single-statement if/for. clang-format -- the tree's
#     formatting source of truth, which runs as its own blocking gate -- is
#     configured to leave those unbraced, so the two gates would contradict
#     each other and no commit could satisfy both.
#
# -modernize-concat-nested-namespaces
#     Wants `namespace avbase::base {` where the tree deliberately writes
#     `namespace avbase {` / `namespace base {` on separate lines. Chromium's
#     style; the split form is what lets each level carry its own comment.
#
# -readability-redundant-member-init
#     Calls `int n_{}` redundant. It is not redundant here: the config also
#     enables cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-member-init, which REQUIRES an
#     initializer. Stripping the braces to satisfy one check trips the other.
#
# These five are the other kind: pure modernisation with no correctness
# payoff, 105 findings between them (return-braced-init-list 44,
# avoid-c-arrays 32, use-auto 17, raw-string-literal 12, use-std-numbers 1).
# `return Foo(x)` vs `return {x}`, a C array vs std::array, an explicit type
# vs auto after a cast -- each is a readability call the project has not made,
# and a blocking gate that forces them turns every review into 105 mechanical
# edits. Nothing here is a bug: bugprone-*, performance-* and
# cppcoreguidelines-* all stay on. If the project does decide to adopt one of
# these spellings it should happen as its own migration round -- `clang-tidy
# -fix` does them mechanically and one build + ctest validates all of them --
# not by holding commits hostage.
#
# -modernize-return-braced-init-list
# -modernize-avoid-c-arrays
# -modernize-use-auto
# -modernize-raw-string-literal
# -modernize-use-std-numbers
#
# -performance-unnecessary-value-param
#     Its advice is backwards for how this tree passes things. The parameters
#     it flags are callback and status arguments -- DecoderStatus, MediaError,
#     scoped_refptr, OnceClosure -- and avbase passes those BY VALUE on purpose
#     because the receiver moves them onward; making them `const&` is what
#     turns that move into a copy. The check cannot see the std::move on the
#     next line. (It also flags plain enums, where by-value is simply smaller
#     than a reference.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  google-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-identifier-naming,
  readability-redundant-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-interfaces-global-init,
  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-member-init,
  misc-unused-*,
  -google-readability-todo,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -performance-enum-size,
  -modernize-use-nodiscard,
  -google-readability-braces-around-statements,
  -modernize-concat-nested-namespaces,
  -readability-redundant-member-init,
  -modernize-return-braced-init-list,
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  -modernize-use-auto,
  -modernize-raw-string-literal,
  -modernize-use-std-numbers,
  -performance-unnecessary-value-param
CheckOptions:
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.StructCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.EnumCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.EnumConstantPrefix: k
  readability-identifier-naming.FunctionCase: CamelCase
  # aNy_CasE here too, and for the same reason as Constant: one clang-tidy
  # category covers three things avbase spells three ways -- a const local
  # (`lower_case`), a const member (`foo_`) and a named constant (`kFoo`).
  # Every setting that fits one rejects another: ConstantPrefix:k flags all 40
  # const locals as wanting a k; leaving Constant unset makes it fall back here
  # and flags every kFoo constant as wanting lower_case; ConstantSuffix:''
  # rejects `max_buffers_`, ConstantSuffix:'_' rejects `local_const`. The
  # category cannot express the distinction, so variable/constant *case* is not
  # enforced and ClassMember (below) keeps only its suffix. Class, Struct,
  # Enum, EnumConstant, Namespace and Parameter are still checked.
  readability-identifier-naming.VariableCase: aNy_CasE
  # Class members carry the trailing underscore; struct data members do NOT.
  # `MemberSuffix` is the convenience alias that sets BOTH, which is why it is
  # not used here: it flagged every field of every POD struct in the tree (533
  # findings in one TU). STYLE.md §2 says "member variable lower_snake_case_"
  # and means the class member -- a struct's public fields are data, not
  # members, exactly as in Chromium.
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassMemberSuffix: _
  # ...but a static constexpr member is a NAMED CONSTANT, not a member: it is
  # spelled kNoLayer / kStatsInterval / kUnixEpochDeltaMicros and carries no
  # trailing underscore. Without this the check classifies it as ClassMember
  # and demands one. (Empty means "no suffix", not "suffix unchecked".)
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassConstantSuffix: ''
  readability-identifier-naming.StructMemberCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.ParameterCase: lower_case
  # aNy_CasE means "do not check this category", and it has to be spelled out:
  # leaving a category unset does NOT disable it, the check falls back to a
  # broader one. Method falls back to Function, so omitting MethodCase
  # re-flagged all 232 accessors as "function".
  #
  # STYLE.md §2.1 makes snake_case() the accessor spelling and CamelCase() the
  # verb spelling -- "snake_case() = reads, CamelCase() = acts". That is a
  # SEMANTIC distinction and readability-identifier-naming can only classify by
  # shape, so any real MethodCase is wrong for half the tree. Naming of methods
  # is left to STYLE.md and review.
  readability-identifier-naming.MethodCase: aNy_CasE
  #
  # Constant gets NO options at all, which is deliberate and is the other half
  # of the fallback lesson: `Constant` covers both const members and const
  # locals, and avbase wants different shapes for them (trailing _ for the
  # member, none for the local). Setting ConstantSuffix to satisfy one breaks
  # the other -- '' rejects `max_buffers_`, '_' rejects `local_const` -- and
  # ConstantCase: aNy_CasE does not help because the suffix still applies.
  # Left unset, a const member falls back to ClassMember (satisfied) and a
  # const local to Variable (satisfied). Genuine named constants are enum
  # constants, and those keep the k prefix above.
  readability-identifier-naming.NamespaceCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.MacroCase: UPPER_CASE
  modernize-use-nullptr.NullMacros: 'NULL'
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
# The leading '/' matters. Without it this is a substring match and "avbase/"
# contains "base/", so every vendored header in the tree was analysed -- 93
# findings inside render/gl/third_party/glad/ alone. It is anchored to a path
# separator so that only avbase's own top-level directories match.
HeaderFilterRegex: '/(base|media|player|platform)/.*\.h$'
FormatStyle: file
